3.1. Conceptual Framework
" immutability is a feature applicable at different layers of a system"
"immutability is less about "cannot change" in the absolute
meaning and more about "should not change"

" rollback is frequently done by simply redeploying previously verified artifacts, and error
correction needs reconciliation rather than deletion"

3.2. Classification Model
"Hard immutability describes a state of being unchangeable where changes are so heavily protected by technical mechanisms
and therefore practically infeasible the alteration process is therefore practically impossible."

"Soft immutability...can be reverted by using privileged credentials."

"Operational immutability implies the lack of changes without the use of technology"

" it is dependent on the team culture, tooling, and adherence. "
"Operational immutability can be
compromised if engineers decide to disregard the process in a situation"

